<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Washington (1871)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1871">1871</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Washington of 1871 settled disputes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a>. It referred the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alabama">Alabama</a> claims over Confederate raiders built in Britain to an international tribunal at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a>, opened fisheries and navigation rights and sent the San Juan Islands boundary to arbitration. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-a-macdonald">John A. Macdonald</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>'s prime minister, signed it as one of the British commissioners.</p></div>
